---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PetMark from '../components/PetMark.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Something went wrong | Perfect Pet Name Generator"
  description="An unexpected error stopped this page from loading. Try again, or head straight to the dog, cat or general pet name generator."
  path="/500/"
  noindex
>
  <div class="wrap py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <span class="flex items-end justify-center gap-3">
        <PetMark pet="dog" size={64} class="pet-mark" style="color: var(--c-dog);" />
        <PetMark pet="cat" size={64} class="pet-mark" style="color: var(--c-cat);" />
      </span>

      <p class="label mt-6" style="letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Error 500</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Something went wrong on our end</h1>

      <p class="mt-4">
        This one is not your fault. An unexpected error stopped the page from loading, and the
        address you used is almost certainly fine. Reloading usually clears it, because these
        failures are nearly always momentary.
      </p>

      <p class="answer-box mt-6 text-left">
        Nothing you typed was affected. Every generator on this site runs entirely in your own
        browser against a static list of names, so no filter, name or household detail you
        entered was ever sent anywhere for this error to lose.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="retry">Try this page again</button>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/">Homepage</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/dog-names/">Dog names</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/cat-names/">Cat names</a>
      </div>

      <p class="hint mt-6">
        Still broken after a reload? <a class="underline" href="/contact/">Let us know</a> and
        include the address you were trying to reach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Reloads whatever the visitor was actually trying to reach. The server may
  // hand this page back under the original URL, in which case reloading retries
  // that URL rather than bouncing the visitor to /500/ itself.
  document.getElementById('retry')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    window.location.reload();
  });
</script>
